# Netlify. One line, and it is the whole SPA refresh fix.
#
# BrowserRouter uses real paths, so /list is a URL the server is asked for -
# and there is no file called "list". Without this rule the host answers 404
# on every refresh and every shared deep link, while clicking around inside
# the app works perfectly. That asymmetry is what makes it confusing.
#
# 200, not 301: serve index.html AT that URL rather than redirecting to "/",
# so the router still sees /list and renders the right route.
/*    /index.html   200
